{"id":"VHH__tool__scalar_crater","collection":"VHH","category":"tool","source_path":"VHH/tool/scalar_crater.json","root_names":["VHH::Tool::scalar_crater"],"counts":{"nodes":99,"connections":172,"values":42,"overloads":1},"documentation_summary":"Component Compound - this compound is a component in the the displacer ecosystem. Scalar Crater - One of the pre-made noise fields. This is a 2d-based (height) field that generates a crater style-displacement. This can get slow.","documentation_search":"scalar crater Component Compound - this compound is a component in the the displacer ecosystem. Scalar Crater - One of the pre-made noise fields. This is a 2d-based (height) field that generates a crater style-displacement. This can get slow. Input mask Scalar field mask on the outgoing field. warp vector field Domain warp on the outgoing field. crater noise Noise to be added to the basic crater paraboloid shape. field weight Overall weight of this field from 0-1. radius The radius of the crater. crater height The height of the crater's cavity. height offset The overall height of the crater walls. rim width The width of the slope that makes up the rim of the crater. rimsteep The steepness of the slope that makes up the rim of the crater. smin Smooth Min, controls the smooth transition between the rim and the crater. smax Smooth Max, controls the smooth transition between the floor and the walls. floor height Controls the floor height of the crater. translate Move the field. rotate Rotate the field. scale Scale the field. invert mask Inverts the scalar field mask. adjust mask A curve input that adjusts the scalar field mask. warp amount The amount to warp the field based on the field used as a domain warp. sharpen When this is selected, the field's opwn gradient is used for a domain warp. At lower values this has the effect of \"sharpening\" the field. step field When this is selected, the field is discretized into \"steps\". step shape The shape of the steps. Because the curve pre- and post-extrapolation is set to \"Relative Repeat\" this acts like a modulo on the field. You can vary the shape of your stepping with just the controls on this curve. step mask A scalar field input to mask area of the step field. invert step mask When this is checked, the step mask is inverted. adjust step mask An fCurve allowing adjustment of the step mask. Output cellular noise field The field result ready to be used.","port_names":["adjust_mask","adjust_step_mask","crater_height","crater_noise","field_weight","floor_height","height_offset","invert_mask","invert_step_mask","mask","output","radius","rim_width","rimsteep","rotation","scale","sharpen","smax","smin","step_field","step_mask","step_shape","translation","warp_amount","warp_vector_field"],"node_types_search":["Core::Conversion::degrees_to_radians","Core::Fields::advect_field","Core::Fields::fcurve_field","Core::Fields::field_is_empty","Core::Fields::gradient_field","Core::Fields::position_field","Core::Fields::scalar_field","Core::Fields::transform_field","Core::Fields::vector_field","Core::Graph::pass","Core::Logic::equal","Core::Logic::if","Core::Math::SRT_to_matrix","Core::Math::add","Core::Math::clamp","Core::Math::divide","Core::Math::euler_to_quaternion","Core::Math::length","Core::Math::lerp","Core::Math::min","Core::Math::multiply","Core::Math::negate","Core::Math::subtract","change_range_field","maskWerks","smoothmax1","smoothmin","step_funct"],"dependencies_search":[],"roots":[{"overload_index":0,"name":"VHH::Tool::scalar_crater","uri_imported":"stream:/bifrostGraphShape1","is_default_overload":null,"metadata":{"documentation":"../docs/scalar_crater.md","_sections":[{"type":"backdrop","title":"Transform"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Make Crater"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Warp"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Masking"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"Field Weight"},{"type":"backdrop","title":"The steps"}]},"documentation_file":"VHH/docs/scalar_crater.md","documentation":"### ***scalar_crater***\n<font size = 1>**Component Compound** - this compound is a component in the the *displacer* ecosystem.<br /><br /></font>\n<font size = 2>**Scalar Crater** - One of the pre-made noise fields.  This is a 2d-based (height) field that generates a crater style-displacement. This can get slow.</font><br />\n\n***\n## Input\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***mask***</span>\n<br />Scalar field mask on the outgoing field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***warp_vector_field***</span>\n<br />Domain warp on the outgoing field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***crater_noise***</span>\n<br />Noise to be added to the basic crater paraboloid shape.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***field_weight***</span>\n<br />Overall weight of this field from 0-1.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***radius***</span>\n<br />The radius of the crater.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***crater_height***</span>\n<br />The height of the crater's cavity.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***height_offset***</span>\n<br />The overall height of the crater walls.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***rim_width***</span>\n<br />The width of the slope that makes up the rim of the crater.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***rimsteep***</span>\n<br />The steepness of the slope that makes up the rim of the crater.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***smin***</span>\n<br />Smooth Min, controls the smooth transition between the rim and the crater.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***smax***</span>\n<br />Smooth Max, controls the smooth transition between the floor and the walls.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***floor_height***</span>\n<br />Controls the floor height of the crater.\n\n<span style=\"color:#A8D977\">***translate***</span>\n<br />Move the field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#A8D977\">***rotate***</span>\n<br />Rotate the field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#A8D977\">***scale***</span>\n<br />Scale the field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#E69963\">***invert_mask***</span>\n<br />Inverts the scalar field mask.\n\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***adjust_mask***</span>\n<br />A curve input that adjusts the scalar field mask.\n\n<span style=\"color:#82D99F\">***warp_amount***</span>\n<br />The amount to warp the field based on the field used as a domain warp.\n\n<span style=\"color:#E69963\">***sharpen***</span>\n<br />When this is selected, the field's opwn gradient is used for a domain warp.  At lower values this has the effect of \"sharpening\" the field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#E69963\">***step_field***</span>\n<br />When this is selected, the field is discretized into \"steps\".\n\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***step_shape***</span>\n<br />The shape of the steps.  Because the curve pre- and post-extrapolation is set to \"Relative Repeat\" this acts like a modulo on the field.  You can vary the shape of your stepping with just the controls on this curve.\n\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***step_mask***</span>\n<br />A scalar field input to mask area of the step field.\n\n<span style=\"color:#E69963\">***invert_step_mask***</span>\n<br />When this is checked, the step_mask is inverted.\n\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***adjust_step_mask***</span>\n<br />An fCurve allowing adjustment of the step_mask.\n\n***\n## Output\n<span style=\"color:#CCB699\">***cellular_noise_field***</span>\n<br />The field result ready to be used.","ports":[{"name":"radius","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"3f"},{"name":"crater_height","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"0f"},{"name":"height_offset","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"2f"},{"name":"rim_width","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"6f"},{"name":"rimsteep","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"0.100000001f"},{"name":"smin","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"15f"},{"name":"smax","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"0.100000001f"},{"name":"floor_height","direction":"input","type":"float","default":"0f"},{"name":"output","direction":"output","type":null},{"name":